<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    GoogleIntegration's cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because the
    section is referenced in both directions: it consumes Humans.Teams.Contracts,
    Humans.Auth.Contracts, Humans.AuditLog.Contracts, Humans.Email.Contracts,
    Humans.Notifications.Contracts and Humans.SystemSettings.Contracts, while Teams,
    Notifications, Surveys and Monitor inject its services. A Contracts/ *folder* inside
    Humans.GoogleIntegration would therefore cycle at the assembly level (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md) — and would cycle a second way, because
    Humans.Application's AuditViewerService and Humans.Infrastructure's SystemTeamSyncJob,
    SuspendNonCompliantMembersJob and HumansMetricsService consume it from Base.

    It holds exactly the eight interfaces something outside the section injects, plus the flat
    projections their signatures name. The rest — the Google API connector abstractions
    (IGoogleDirectoryClient, IGoogleDrivePermissionsClient, ITeamResourceGoogleClient, …),
    IGoogleAdminService, IGoogleWorkspaceUserService, ISyncSettingsService and
    IGoogleRemovalNotificationService — have no consumer outside
    Humans.{Application,Infrastructure,Web} and stay with the section.

    Two absences are load-bearing. ISystemTeamSync is NOT here: it syncs system-team
    membership, names Google nowhere in its signature, and its implementation
    (SystemTeamSyncJob) is a cross-section orchestrator in Humans.Infrastructure. Putting it
    on this leaf would have made Auth — a horizontal — reference a vertical section, which
    peters-hard-rules.md forbids; leaving it in Base keeps Auth, Development, Governance and
    Onboarding off this leaf entirely. And IDriveActivityMonitorService is not here because it
    moved to Humans.Monitor for the same reason, one lane earlier.

    IGoogleGroupSync is here despite having no *section* consumer: SystemTeamSyncJob injects
    it from Base, and a Base file cannot reference the section project. If that job ever moves
    into a section, this interface goes back to internal.

    References Humans.Interfaces (IApplicationService, ExternalWriteAttribute) and Humans.Domain
    (GoogleResourceType, DrivePermissionLevel, SyncAction, and the GoogleResource /
    GoogleSyncOutboxEvent entities two members still expose — an existing leak recorded on the
    debt ledger, not introduced here), the same pair Humans.Teams.Contracts and
    Humans.Campaigns.Contracts take. Acyclic: Humans.Domain names only Humans.Interfaces.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Domain\Humans.Domain.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
